course: dictionary
lesson: 3083
title: Educated: what the word tells you
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Educated» can describe a person who has learned a lot, often at school, college or university. «Educated people in Columbus's time already knew the Earth was round.» Here it means people who knew a lot about the world, not just people who had been to school.
explain: «Educated» can also be a verb form, the past of «educate», meaning taught: «She was educated at a school in Dublin.» Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits. Is the sentence about what someone knows, or about what someone was given?
explain: An «educated guess» is a guess based on what you already know, not a wild guess. In science you might make one before an experiment, using facts you have learned to predict what will happen.
fact: Educated means having learned a lot, especially at school, college or university.
fact: «Well educated» and «highly educated» both praise someone who knows a lot.
fact: An «educated guess» is based on some knowledge; a wild guess is based on nothing much at all.
fact: «Educated Europeans knew the Earth was round since ancient Greek times.»
fact: «Columbus thought the Earth was much smaller than it is.»
exercise: «Educated people already knew the Earth was round.» What does educated mean here? | *People who had learned a lot | People who had a lot of money | People who lived near the sea | People who were very tired
exercise: In science you might make an «educated guess» before an experiment. What is an educated guess? | A guess a teacher makes for you | A guess made with your eyes shut | A guess that is always wrong | *A guess based on some knowledge
exercise: «She was educated at a school in Dublin.» What does educated mean in this sentence? | *Was taught, given lessons | Finished her homework early | Felt angry at the school | Moved away from the city
test: Which phrase praises someone who knows a lot? | Sad and glum | *Well educated | Fast runner | Wild guess
test: Why is an educated guess different from a wild guess? | It is always right | *It uses what you already know | It is longer to say | It is made without thinking at all
exam: Which meaning fits «a highly educated doctor»? | *A doctor who has learned a lot | A doctor who works only at night | A doctor who was born in Dublin | A doctor who is very tall
